    ["廷根街头， 病重的青年艾德请你帮忙买一枚戒指、一束百合，前往书店替他回绝笔友。你购物后来到书店，藏在书柜旁等待，却看见一个糙汉大叔取走了礼物。惊讶之时，警察突然出现，揭露装病行骗是诈骗团伙的惯用伎俩。最讽刺的是，艾德装病许久，入狱体检时才发现自己真的身患重疾。骗子终将落网，而命运从不开玩笑。"] = "On the streets of Tingen, a seriously ill young man named Ed asks you to help him buy a ring and a bouquet of lilies to go to the bookstore and reject a pen pal on his behalf. After shopping, you arrive at the bookstore and hide beside the bookshelf to wait, but you see a rough-looking man take the gifts. Just as you are surprised, the police appear, revealing that faking illness is a common tactic used by fraud gangs. The most ironic thing is that Ed had been faking illness for a long time, and it was only during the prison medical examination that he discovered he was truly suffering from a serious illness. The scammers will eventually be caught, and fate never jokes.",
